# Security headers for every response.
#
# Cache-Control is deliberately NOT set on /*: Cloudflare merges matching
# blocks by *appending* header values rather than replacing them, so a
# Cache-Control here would be prepended to the asset rules below and win
# (RFC 9110: the first max-age occurrence takes precedence), silently
# disabling all asset caching.
#
# Per-page HTML rules are appended by scripts/build-dist.mjs. They have to be
# generated because the canonical URLs are extensionless (/about, not
# /about.html - every .html URL 301-redirects via _redirects), so a /*.html
# rule would never match a real request. Cloudflare allows 100 rules in total;
# the build script stays inside that budget and warns instead of breaking the
# deploy if the site ever outgrows it.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()

/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000, stale-while-revalidate=86400
